\section*{Question 3}
\begin{itemize}
\item[] Let \(R\) be the region in the first quadrant bounded by the \(y\)-axis and the graphs of \(y=4 x-x^{3}+1\) and \(y=\frac{3}{4} x\).
\item[(a)] Find the area of \(R\).
\item[(b)] Find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is revolved about the \(x\)-axis.
(c) Write an expression involving one or more integrals that gives the perimeter of \(R\). Do not evaluate.
